course: dictionary
lesson: 8107
title: Rennet and cheese
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rennet is a noun for a thing, and it is uncountable, so you say some rennet, not two rennets. It is a substance that makes milk go thick and lumpy so that it can become cheese. «Cheese-makers add bacteria and rennet to milk, which separates into solid curds and watery whey.»
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. The milk separates into solid curds and watery whey, and the curds become cheese. So rennet must be a helper that makes the milk set into lumps. Test your meaning in the sentence: cheese-makers add a helper that makes milk set into lumps, and that still makes sense.
explain: Rennet can come from different places. Traditional rennet comes from a calf's stomach, so it is animal rennet. Vegetable or microbial rennet is made from plants or microbes, and it is used for vegetarian cheese. That is why vegetarians check cheese labels.
fact: Rennet is a substance that makes milk curdle, which means it goes thick and lumpy.
fact: «Curds» are the soft lumps of thickened milk, and «whey» is the watery liquid left behind.
fact: Traditional rennet comes from a calf's stomach, so it is called animal rennet.
fact: Vegetable and microbial rennet are made from plants or microbes, and they are used for vegetarian cheese.
fact: Rennet is uncountable, so you say «some rennet», not «two rennets».
exercise: «Cheese-makers add bacteria and rennet to milk.» What does rennet do to the milk? | It makes it hotter | It turns it into water | It makes it fizzy like lemonade | *It makes it set into thick, lumpy curds
exercise: «Little Miss Muffet ate curds and whey.» Which word means the watery liquid left over? | Ate | *Whey | Miss | Curds
exercise: Why do vegetarians check cheese labels for rennet? | Rennet is always made from fruit | Rennet is a type of bread | *Animal rennet comes from a calf's stomach | Cheese never contains rennet
test: Which phrase uses rennet correctly? | Two rennets | A rennets | Three rennet | *Some rennet
test: Which kind of rennet is suitable for vegetarian cheese? | Whey | Animal rennet from a calf | Curds | *Vegetable or microbial rennet
exam: Rennet makes milk separate into which two parts? | Bread and water | *Curds and whey | Yoghurt and milk | Cheese and butter
